    "body": "(Sorry, forgot to name the issue 😅 )\n\nI think the changes in #11725 don't change anything here. Still, firing the push/replace event aborts the ongoing event, which triggers a new navigate, which tries to set the upcoming API method tracker, before the original push/replace event code enters the inner navigate firing algorithm, which promotes the upcoming API method tracker to ongoing.",
