    "created_at": "2025-10-06T08:40:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-06T08:40:39Z",
    "body": "That doesn't sound right. Wouldn't this imply that the third navigate would set the upcoming API method tracker, would then get aborted by the second one as soon as its `navigate()` returns, and then the second one would continue with the API method tracker of the (aborted) third one? That would be a broken state.\n\nI think this is a deeper issue. The abort loop allows to run script, but the internal navigation state is not \"clean\" -- therefore the script could mess up the internal navigation state, which is what happens in this test. Maybe we can solve this by moving the [promoting step](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#inner-navigate-event-firing-algorithm:~:text=Promote%20an%20upcoming%20API%20method%20tracker%20to%20ongoing%20given%20navigation%20and%20destinationKey%2E) to run before the abort loop (but this could have other implications I don't see atm). Or we could move the current state into a temporary before running the abort loop (that sounds a bit hacky tho).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
