    "created_at": "2025-10-06T20:19:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-06T20:19:22Z",
    "body": "> Maybe we can solve this by moving the [promoting step](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#inner-navigate-event-firing-algorithm:~:text=Promote%20an%20upcoming%20API%20method%20tracker%20to%20ongoing%20given%20navigation%20and%20destinationKey%2E) to run before the abort loop (but this could have other implications I don't see atm).\n\nYeah, this causes a bunch of WPT to assert in chromium, and is enough of an ordering change that I'm jumpy about it.\n\n> Or we could move the current state into a temporary before running the abort loop (that sounds a bit hacky tho).\n\nAgreed that it's a bit hacky, but it fixes the issue. [This WIP CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7013335) transfers the tracker to a tempoary and adds the assert to chromium, and it passes WPT. Though it makes [promote an upcoming API method tracker to ongoing](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#promote-an-upcoming-api-method-tracker-to-ongoing) look strange enough that maybe it should be inlined [at its sole invocation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/nav-history-apis.html#navigate-event-firing:promote-an-upcoming-api-method-tracker-to-ongoing).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
